WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.840
- Give it up for my band y'all,

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.690
as I was saying, everybody.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.940
That song was Walkaway Joe,

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.770
by Mrs.Trisha Yearwood and Don Henley.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:14.600
I love Trisha Yearwood y'all, seriously

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.160
one of my favorite singers on the planet.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.300
Let's meet Matthew who
requested that song.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.723
So where are you at Matthew?

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:21.610
- Austin, Texas

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.554
- It's Matthew McConaughey!

00:00:22.554 --> 00:00:24.387
- How you doing Kelly?

00:00:26.854 --> 00:00:28.390
- How are you doing?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.840
- Relatively pretty well,

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.980
we're trying to get over
this freeze down here,

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.180
you know, it kind of knocked
some of us back a hair

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.240
but overall we're doing pretty good.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.073
- Yeah. Oh my God.

00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:38.600
That's good to hear, that's good to hear.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.630
Why did you request Walkway Joe?

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.160
- Well, Walkaway Joe, and it
was, think it was early 1992,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:48.460
I'm going to college here
at the University of Texas.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:50.560
This is before Dazed and Confused,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.590
and I was trying to get odd jobs

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.750
in front of the camera when I could.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.750
And I got cast in that
music video to play Joe.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.330
Things are going well then where

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.580
we ended up at the last
stop, she wakes up,

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.780
and "Joe", myself, is nowhere to be seen.

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:09.670
Therefore, AKA the title, Walkaway Joe.

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.350
- I love that though, don't you remember?

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.290
I love that about country
music videos, especially

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.730
in like the nineties, there
would be such a story,

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:17.460
like a plot, they'd have actors,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:19.710
really big actors, and
I think that's amazing.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:20.810
I didn't know that was your first thing.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.600
I didn't know that was
before Dazed and Confused.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:23.590
It's amazing.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.190
- That, and Unsolved Mysteries.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:28.190
Yeah. Walkaway Joe was my first
time in front of the camera.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.349
And I still don't believe
I've met Trisha in person.

00:01:32.349 --> 00:01:35.023
- Did you just say that
and unsolved mysteries?

00:01:35.945 --> 00:01:36.778
- [Matthew] Yes.

00:01:36.778 --> 00:01:39.357
I love you so much! That's amazing.

00:01:39.357 --> 00:01:42.900
Not that I'm complaining, because
I love you, everyone does,

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.230
but what are you doing
here in our audience?

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:47.568
- I am here in your audience today

00:01:47.568 --> 00:01:51.110
because as you know, as
I mentioned a minute ago,

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:55.210
our state, Texas, was hit
by the worst freeze it's had

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:58.320
in over 70 years and
Texans were without power.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.250
There's still a lot of
them without clean water.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:02.950
They have major water damage
some are without food.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.480
Some can't move back into their homes.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.610
Kids can't go back to the schools.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.480
And myself and Camila are hosting

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:13.910
and throwing a We Are
Texas virtual concert.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.900
That's going to be on my YouTube channel

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.870
on March 21st at 7:00
PM, central Texas time.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.350
As my brother calls it, "real time",

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.300
and we got a hell of a
show we're gonna put out.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.260
We've got a lot of great performers.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.540
I'm calling it a
restoration Texas concert.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:30.530
It's going to be a revival.

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:31.760
It's not going to be a sob show.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.410
It's going to be a jam
session of generosity.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:36.310
- I love that.

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:39.460
I love, I actually, I was
very excited that you asked me

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:40.920
to be a part of it because one,

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.240
it's a really cool thing to
be able to have a spotlight

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.300
like you have in the industry.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.600
And then you get to use it for good.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.050
When it really counts and matters.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.530
And also then I love that you made it more

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:52.730
of an uplifting thing of
just jamming out instead

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:55.300
of just such a somber
thing, because it's already

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.610
been kind of a melancholy moment,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.020
the past year and a half.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.460
And so I think it was really important.

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.132
So what organizations are
you raising money for?

00:03:04.132 --> 00:03:05.760
- A hundred percent of the donations,

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:09.060
meaning 100 cents on every dollar donated.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.020
Is going to go through our

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.720
Just Keep Living Foundation:
Texas Relief Fund.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.120
And it's going to go to
organizations all over Texas,

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:19.100
in the urban areas and in
the rural parts of Texas.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.920
places like St.Bernard Project,

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:23.150
Team Rubicon on the
ground, Save the Children,

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:26.850
Austin Disaster Relief, Meals
on Wheels to name a few.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.720
These are organizations that
are helping out real needs

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.020
that are fixable with the right donations

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:33.200
right now in Texas.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.320
- Absolutely are fixable.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.340
I love that.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:38.450
And honestly, I was
excited to watch it myself

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.165
and be able to be a part of it because

00:03:40.165 --> 00:03:44.460
the guest list of people
coming it's so random.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.670
- [Matthew] Well, that was
one of the cool things.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:48.840
I mean, the lineup is
pure Texas and it's deep.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.180
You know, like I said,
you've got yourself.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.140
You've got Don Henley.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.876
You got Gary Clark Jr, George
Strait, Kacey Musgraves,

00:03:54.876 --> 00:03:58.190
you, Khalid, Kirk Franklin, Leon Bridges,

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:00.390
Lucas Nelson, Lyle
Lovett, Miranda Lambert,

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.460
Parker McCollum, Post Malone,
Randy Rogers, Willie Nelson.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.570
I mean, that's all Texas talent,

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.610
and we couldn't even fit
in all the Texas talent.

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:11.590
So it's going to be a
hell of a fun night and

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.686
all those musicians cover quite
a few genres of good music.

00:04:14.686 --> 00:04:16.550
- Yeah, that's what I'm
saying it's an amazing thing

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.140
because that's another
thing I love about Texas,

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:20.270
and everybody will come
together and it will get fixed.

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.430
And you said this is a fixable situation,

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:23.263
all these situations.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.420
And I love that about Texans.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.970
We are so random, like the
set list of people there,

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:30.128
it's such a random variety of people,

00:04:30.128 --> 00:04:32.220
but I think that's
what's cool about Texas,

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:33.300
is it doesn't matter where you come from,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.470
everybody's invited to the party

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.030
and everybody's welcome to join in,

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.760
and everybody wants to help everybody,

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:39.740
that's why I love
growing up in that state.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.700
But what else can people do
help each other down there?

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.890
- Well, I wanted to bring
up another cool thing

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:45.180
and you know this as a Texan,

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.046
and this is a really
cool thing about Texas.

00:04:47.046 --> 00:04:51.570
Texans, we like to help ourselves.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:53.110
And what we're going to
be doing with this relief,

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:56.280
with this benefit is donations
are going to be helping

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.070
out people that want to help themselves

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:01.200
and are trying to help
themselves, but are unable to.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.460
And boy, that's a great way.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.920
To anyone out there wants to
give know that you're giving it

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:07.140
to people who have already
pulled their bootstraps up.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.740
And they're saying, I'm
trying to help myself.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.660
I'm just having trouble doing so.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:12.800
- Yeah. Absolutely, absolutely.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.780
What else can people
do to help down there?

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:16.813
Like other than obviously be
a part of the virtual benefit

00:05:16.813 --> 00:05:18.550
and be a part and donate money?

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.090
What else do you think people should

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.410
- [Matthew] Look, time.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.210
You know, people in Texas right now

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.000
let's remind everyone
out there right now is

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.250
no better time than to go
knock on your neighbor's door

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:31.660
or see if someone else is having trouble

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:33.860
around in your neighborhood,
in your community.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.480
There's plenty of help to go around.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.920
So if you can give your time,

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.450
if you can give a little effort,

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.700
even going by to see
somebody, we've got stories

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.450
of people that had their door knocked on,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.270
that people just hadn't talked to anybody,

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:46.920
they've been stuck in their
home with water damage

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.760
and not even gone out and
to see a neighbor come by

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.713
and just check on them,
meant something to them.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.310
So keep your ears open and eyes open

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.430
around your own neighborhoods,

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.570
people need it all over the state.

00:05:58.570 --> 00:06:00.770
And if there's a way you can also

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:03.110
donate your time in the long run,

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.690
we're talking to people like
Team Rubicon, more people.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.810
If you don't want to
donate a dollar or five,

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.940
or however much, you can donate
your time to go help people

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:12.780
on the ground in Texas here too.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:13.690
- [Kelly] That's so great.

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:16.940
What's an example of
something you've seen,

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.710
one Texan doing for
another through all this?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.180
I know there's gotta be plenty.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:23.370
- Yeah. Yeah. And this parlays
off of what I was just saying

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:26.520
about how these Texans are people

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:29.240
who want to help
themselves, but need help.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:30.670
And these donations are
going to help those people

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:31.940
that want to help themselves.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.180
There's for instance, there's this lady

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.700
in Houston and she's an older lady,

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.093
but very young in spirit and pure Texan.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.648
She gets up the morning after the freeze

00:06:42.648 --> 00:06:44.330
and she heads out into a neighborhood

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:47.440
and she starts helping out
her neighbors who had damage.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.330
And I mean, she's in the middle of it

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.850
getting dirty, helping out.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.220
She gets up the next
day, she does it again.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.670
We hear about this story.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.658
We went down to go cover her,
neighbors helping neighbors.

00:06:57.658 --> 00:06:59.330
Wow, isn't this a great story.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.490
Somebody who's helping out a neighbor.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:03.200
Only to find out that that night,

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.395
when we followed her home to her apartment

00:07:05.395 --> 00:07:07.850
her apartment had busted water lines,

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.740
flooding, collapsed ceilings.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.960
And she was like, Oh, I
wasn't even bringing that up.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.400
I was going to help somebody else out

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:16.320
that I think maybe
needed more help than me.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:19.620
And she needed help, and she
wouldn't even ask for help.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.030
- Oh that's so Texan.

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:22.830
- So I helped people like that as well.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.670
- That's amazing that she had
this, God, what a great heart.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.503
Wow.

00:07:28.503 --> 00:07:29.336
- Right?

00:07:29.336 --> 00:07:31.010
For more information
on how you can help go

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.770
to our Instagram story or
check out Matthew's Instagram

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:37.170
and to watch the We Are Texas
Virtual Benefit Concert go

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:40.000
to Matthew's YouTube page on March 21st.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.530
Thank you so much for being
here, Matthew, we love you.

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:43.810
Thank you so much.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.300
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:47.180
Thank you for your performance
too, with the show.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:49.170
We're going to do a lot of
good for a lot of good people.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.120
- [Kelly] Oh man. I hope so, I hope so.

